    "title": "Texas man killed in Shelby County crash - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By AJ Holliday ,\n1 days ago\nSHELBY COUNTY, Ala. ( WIAT ) — A two-vehicle crash near Shelby County 22 left a man from Texas dead Monday night.\nMelvin Alvarado, 32, of Conroe, Tx., was killed when the motorcycle he was driving collided head-on with a Nissan Pathfinder around 6:57 p.m. Alvarado was thrown from the motorcycle and was pronounced dead at the scene. The driver of the Pathfinder was transported to Baptist Health Shelby Hospital in Alabaster for treatment.\nNothing else is available as Alabama Law Enforcement Agency continues to investigate.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CBS 42.",
    "summary": "SHELBY COUNTY, Ala. ( WIAT ) — A two-vehicle crash near Shelby County 22 left a man from Texas dead Monday night. Melvin Alvarado, 32, of Conroe, Tx., was killed when the motorcycle he was driving collided head-on with a Nissan Pathfinder around 6:57 p.m. Alvarado was thrown from the motorcycle and was pronounced dead at the scene. The driver of the Pathfinder was transported to Baptist Health Shelby Hospital in Alabaster for treatment. Nothing else is available as Alabama Law Enforcement Agency continues to investigate. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CBS 42.",
